WEBVTT

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.860
<i>There are happy stories.</i>

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.270
<i>There are sad legends.</i>

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.360
<i>There are wonderful tales 
that will warm your heart.</i>

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.320
<i>There are unbearably horrible stories.</i>

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.180
<i>There are ghost stories that will keep 
you from sleeping a wink at night.</i>

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.180
<i>Comedies that will make you burst 
into laughter with just a single glance.</i>

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.460
<i>In so many languages, in so many forms,</i>

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.610
<i>there are stories everywhere you look.</i>

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.520
<i>Before there was written language,</i>

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.790
<i>there were songs, oral traditions,</i>

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.480
<i>treasures passed from 
one generation to the next.</i>

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:45.960
<i>Everything in the world...</i>

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:50.930
<i>is recorded by books.</i>

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.640
<i>People experience the world through books.</i>

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:02.080
<i>To write their own stories...</i>

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.350
<i>They keep going forward every day.</i>

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:43.010
<b>Episode 1: 
Story Syndrome</b>

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.310
<i>Kagimura Hazuki has no friends.</i>

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:51.600
<i>I don't mean she has few friends, 
or even very few friends,</i>

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:56.560
<i>or she has some people she knows, 
but she's not sure if she can call them "friends."</i>

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:59.010
<i>It's nothing so pleasant as that...</i>

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:01.950
Okay, let's see...

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:06.640
<i>And she's most certainly not 
a harem light novel character,</i>

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.060
<i>with no friends but many lovers.</i>

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:13.820
<i>She's 16 years old right now, 
and she has absolutely no...</i>

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.110
Kagimura Hazuki!

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.140
<i>She has absolutely no friends. Not a single one.</i>

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:28.970
<b>Teacher's Office</b>

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.480
You need to focus more.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:35.860
Yes, sir...

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.160
Your three years in high school 
may seem long, but they're not.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:40.450
Yes, sir...

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:43.270
You should work harder 
to fit in with the class...

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.770
Did you join a club?

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:53.160
No...

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.040
Excuse me...

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:05.160
You got called to the teacher's office again?

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.020
Seriously?

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:10.640
What do you have to do 
to end up here once a week?

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:11.770
I-I'm sorry.

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:13.520
Misa, you're so harsh!

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.650
Stop acting so afraid.

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.740
You're making it look like I'm bullying you.

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:18.730
I'm sorry.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:19.980
I just said—

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:20.950
Misa, stop.

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:23.120
Your sister's really scared.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:25.710
<i>Oh, no...</i>

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.660
<i>It's starting again!</i>

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:29.970
I'm sorry!

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:30.950
She's fast!

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:42.900
Station Book Store

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:45.970
I-I'll take these!

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:01.940
<i>I've got a bad habit.</i>

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:04.420
<i>Whenever something 
unpleasant or painful happens,</i>

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:08.050
<i>I escape into the world of books... of stories.</i>

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.990
<i>Story Syndrome.</i>

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:19.770
<i>That's what I call this bad habit of mine.</i>

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:43.110
<b>Saeko-san</b>

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.110
<i>Sure,</i>

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.820
<i>I want to get along with my new family.</i>

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:50.960
Hazuki-san,

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:54.220
I told you that you didn't 
need to do the laundry, right?

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.050
I'm paying good money for those cleaners.

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:58.930
Let them do it.

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:01.790
<i>Saeko-san makes fashion books 
at a publishing company.</i>

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:03.520
<i>Supposedly, she's very important.</i>

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:09.430
<i>And Misa-san is the perfect image
 of a social teenage girl.</i>

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:12.360
<i>Oh, no! Look at the time.</i>

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:13.860
<i>I'll be home late tonight,</i>

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:16.230
<i>so get some food somewhere.</i>

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:18.230
Okay, got it.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:21.280
<i>And don't spend too much time 
with your nose in a book.</i>

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:31.550
I want to get along with everyone, too...

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.830
Look, your bow tie's messed up.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.380
Sister!

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:41.400
That's not quite right!

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:50.540
<i>In my fantasies, it's easy to talk to them.</i>

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:52.620
At times like this, I need a book!

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:53.720
I'll read a book!

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:56.430
Huh?

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.800
I didn't buy this book...

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.570
Maybe it's a book of magic?

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:07.340
Huh?

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:34.270
You can't get my hopes up 
and then do that to me!

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:00.700
Huh?

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:21.310
<i>Other people can't see her?</i>

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:28.510
<i>Is that...</i>

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:30.870
<i>That's right!</i>

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:32.870
<i>I know that robe!</i>

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:37.500
<i>She's... She's a real...</i>

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:49.920
<i>She's gone.</i>

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:52.550
Don't move.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:56.970
You can see me, can't you?

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:57.950
Who are you?

00:08:57.950 --> 00:08:59.260
No. What do you want?

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:01.350
I-I...

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:02.390
I like you!

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:06.360
No, that's not it...

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:07.770
I mean, it's not <i>not</i> it...

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:09.980
But I don't mean you, specifically...

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:12.940
But that doesn't mean I don't like you...

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:17.040
What I'm trying to say is...

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:17.920
Friends!

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:18.530
Yes!

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:20.950
Would you like to be friends?

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:24.070
What are you talking about?

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:28.690
Anyway, if you keep following me, 
I'll show you no mercy!

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:40.960
My phone!

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:45.590
She forgot her bag.

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:51.400
<i>Real magic!</i>

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.760
<i>A real mage!</i>

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.410
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:03.440
<i>It wasn't just in books!</i>

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:15.860
A library?

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:39.950
I can't believe I wouldn't know 
about an amazing library like this.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:41.860
No, that's not what's important!

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:45.450
<i>She's here.</i>

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:47.540
<i>That's what the pounding 
of my heart is telling me.</i>

00:10:59.050 --> 00:10:59.980
Maerchen.

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:18.640
Th-This must be the entrance 
to the world of magic!

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:21.500
Maybe I've learned an incredible secret!

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:25.760
Um... Um...

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:30.580
<i>I think my mother is 
the reason I'm like this.</i>

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:35.110
<i>She told me all kinds of stories.</i>

00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:37.490
<i>Not just famous stories.</i>

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:40.590
<i>She had a lot of stories she made herself.</i>

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:44.090
<i>And at the end of each story, 
she'd always say the same thing.</i>

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:49.540
Hazuki, find your own story.

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:56.780
<i>When I was little,</i>

00:11:56.780 --> 00:12:00.030
<i>I thought about the meaning 
of those words as hard as I could.</i>

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:07.700
<i>I thought and thought and thought some more,</i>

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.850
<i>and what I ended up with were my fantasies.</i>

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:13.780
<i>Everything I encountered 
became fuel for my fantasies.</i>

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.040
<i>Those fantasies lead to more fantasies,</i>

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:20.720
<i>and they all got mixed up together.</i>

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:21.720
<i>But...</i>

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:30.980
<i>I knew, on some level,</i>

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:34.270
<i>that I couldn't go to that world.</i>

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.880
<i>No matter how many fantasies I came up with,</i>

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:46.270
<i>I was me. I couldn't be anything else.</i>

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:51.190
<i>All Kagimura Hazuki had waiting 
for her was an ordinary,</i>

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:53.860
<i>unchanging life that would go on forever.</i>

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:56.480
Oh, right!

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:58.400
She said a magic spell!

00:12:58.400 --> 00:12:59.520
What was it?

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:00.920
Um...

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:04.110
<i>But that was wrong!</i>

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:05.780
<i>The other world was real!</i>

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:11.410
Please! Open!

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:13.880
I want to be friends with her!

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:22.210
The book...

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:24.450
No way!

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:26.470
Wow! I'm incredible!

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:39.130
Wait. I think maybe I want 
to go home first, after all!

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:41.270
Then I'll talk to Saeko-san first,

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:43.760
eat dinner, do my homework, 
take a bath, read a book...

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.170
And then, and then...

00:14:10.770 --> 00:14:12.770
Excuse me!

00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:14.590
Is anyone home?

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:17.320
Is it okay to just walk in?

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.960
I've never seen that uniform.

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.600
Who are you with?

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:26.130
I-I'm...

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.790
Wait. Is this a school?

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:31.870
Not a castle for mages?

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:35.880
Th-Those are the eyes of a thug!

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:37.620
Jump harder!

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:42.360
You're suspicious.

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:44.820
Especially that thing you're carrying.

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:47.070
Y-You can't have this!

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:49.670
I have to give it to the mage!

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:52.280
B...

00:14:52.730 --> 00:14:53.780
B?

00:14:54.650 --> 00:14:56.040
Bye!

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:56.040
So fast!

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:57.310
Hold it!

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:06.250
<i>I'm unbelievably bad at sports,</i>

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.600
<i>but running is one thing I'm pretty good at.</i>

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:12.180
<i>It's because I spend 
so much of my time running.</i>

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:17.440
Um... Where am I?

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:30.980
Oh, a visitor. How rare!

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:36.300
It's been so long since any 
students have come out here.

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:39.320
What Original did you contract with?

00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:41.870
Want one?

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:43.430
No, thank you!

00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:45.760
Forget that. I met this girl...

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:47.340
I wanted to give her 
something she dropped.

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:49.590
I chased after her, and there 
was the entrance to a library,

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:52.030
and the next thing I knew, 
I was here... And um...

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:52.960
I see.

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:54.300
So that's it.

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:55.790
So that's what happened.

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:02.840
U-Um...

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:05.150
It's been a long time 
since I've had a visitor.

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:08.010
I want to welcome you properly.

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:11.450
The art of properly welcoming someone 
is one of the Japanese virtues, right?

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:16.290
My little retreat here has delicious tea 
and pickled vegetables picked from the fields,

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:18.270
as well as this open-air bath.

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:20.290
Relax and enjoy yourself.

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:22.160
R-Right...

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:23.570
Um...

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:24.710
What is it?

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:27.050
The girl who dropped this

00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:30.670
is a student at the school 
that's like a castle, right?

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:31.740
Yeah.

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:34.760
The olive-colored robe is one 
of the school's official uniforms.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:38.520
The rule is that when we go 
to the other side, we always wear it.

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:40.860
So this really is a magic...

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:42.120
Wait.

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:44.060
Now it's my turn to ask questions.

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:46.820
Is this book yours?

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:48.900
Yes.

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:51.300
Well, I guess...

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:54.810
It was just kind of in my bag.

00:16:54.810 --> 00:16:57.130
I see. So that's it.

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:59.490
Interesting. This is interesting!

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:04.240
Um... Can you explain 
so I'll understand, as well?

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:05.970
What is that book?

00:17:05.970 --> 00:17:07.180
Or that library?

00:17:07.180 --> 00:17:08.820
Where am I?

00:17:11.100 --> 00:17:12.460
Um...

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:19.220
Wh-What?

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:28.400
I finally found you.

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:31.890
You wandered in from 
the other side, didn't you?

00:17:31.890 --> 00:17:35.110
If that's the case, there's no way 
the principal wouldn't notice.

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:39.100
Which means someone invited you.

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:42.080
I was right.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.790
She's gone?!

00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:46.350
I-I have to run!

00:17:46.350 --> 00:17:48.160
But first, my clothes...

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:49.210
My clothes are gone!

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:50.390
Clothes are gone!

00:17:50.390 --> 00:17:51.320
Book is here!

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:52.170
What is this?

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:55.800
Th-That pretty woman must've taken them...

00:17:58.250 --> 00:18:00.300
This time, I won't let you go!

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:05.100
<i>Question: What do you do if you 
need to run or you're going to die,</i>

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:08.770
<i>but you're totally naked, 
not even wearing underwear?</i>

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:12.780
<i>Note: You have no clothes, 
but you do have a fairly large book.</i>

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:16.740
Wait!

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:22.300
Why are you following me?

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:25.540
Because you keep running!

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:33.300
I've got you!

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:34.040
Ow...

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:35.450
Um... Um...

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:38.630
Is that book an Original?

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:39.840
That would mean...

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:41.470
Stop, damn it!

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:56.180
I said to stop running!

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:58.210
No!

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:09.980
Where am I?

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:22.260
Training was hard today.

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:26.140
I wonder if I can get an Original 
to accept me like the older girls.

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:27.410
Who's that?

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:28.380
Where are her clothes!

00:19:28.380 --> 00:19:29.440
N-No!

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:30.790
I-I'm...

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:36.450
You're in the way!

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:37.570
Move!

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:40.540
Aren't you embarrassed going around naked?

00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:41.720
Whose fault is that?

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:44.310
If you need clothes, use your Original.

00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:45.380
Original?

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:48.550
Here I go.

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:49.960
Shuten Douji!

00:19:59.620 --> 00:20:03.020
Let's see the power of that thing...

00:20:04.030 --> 00:20:07.390
If you don't want to die, use your Original!

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:10.310
<i>I finally made it to the land of magic, but...</i>

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:12.600
<i>And... and...</i>

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:16.560
No, that's not it...

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:18.030
I mean, it's not <i>not</i> it...

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:20.240
But I don't mean you, specifically...

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:23.200
But that doesn't mean I don't like you...

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:27.430
What I'm trying to say is...

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:28.260
Friends!

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:28.790
Yes!

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:31.330
Would you like to be friends?

00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:36.790
<i>I haven't made friends with that mage yet.</i>

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:39.340
I won't allow this kind 
of behavior at my school.

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:46.680
Yumilia Qazan.

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:48.160
What is your problem?

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:50.360
Don't get so mad.

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:53.130
I just scared her a little.

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:00.610
I finally got to see it, huh?

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:03.330
Don't tell me you...

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:05.000
You're a Maedchen?

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:06.000
Um...

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.070
I-I'm...

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:10.300
Hey!

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:14.390
Somebody tell the principal!

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:19.800
<i>Welcome to my school, new Maedchen.</i>

00:21:22.150 --> 00:21:24.500
<i>"What's a Maedchen?"</i>

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.590
Wake up!

00:21:26.980 --> 00:21:31.950
<i>That's what I thought about
 in my fuzzy mind...</i>

00:23:06.400 --> 00:23:07.230
It's me, Hazuki!

00:23:07.230 --> 00:23:08.750
It's me, Tsuchimikado Shizuka.

00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:10.280
It's time for the preview, Shizuka-chan!

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:14.090
I must prepare myself to 
accomplish this great task.

00:23:14.090 --> 00:23:15.380
For the honor of the Tsuchimikado clan...

00:23:15.380 --> 00:23:17.420
No, it's not that big of a deal...

00:23:17.420 --> 00:23:20.280
Each time I trip over my tongue, 
one member of the clan dies.

00:23:20.280 --> 00:23:21.450
Everyone is prepared.

00:23:21.450 --> 00:23:22.970
Th-That's way too big of a deal!

00:23:22.970 --> 00:23:24.880
Next time: First Magic.

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Episode 2: 
First Magic</b>

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:27.510
The survival of the clan depends on me!

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:29.030
Watch over me, mother!

00:23:29.030 --> 00:23:31.160
I don't want to do a preview like this!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.310
<b>Illustration: Rumi Abeshima</b>
